    "evidence_text": "List of Skittles products\n\nSkittles candy products, produced by the Wm. Wrigley Jr.\n\n Company, come in a wide variety.\n\n The oldest Skittles product is Original Fruit Skittles, which was originally released in Europe in 1974, and was launched in the United States in 1979.\n\n Earlier Skittles products tended to focus on fruit flavors, more recent products have branched out to include flavors such as chocolate, bubble gum, popcorn, mint, and sours.\n\nSkittles (confectionery)\n\nSkittles is a brand of fruit-flavoured sweets, currently produced and marketed by the Wrigley Company, a division of Mars, Inc..\n\nGreater Boston\n\nMorattab\n\n It was founded in 1973 by Earnie Larson and is currently headquartered in Kemp, Texas, United States.\n\n Headquartered in McLean, unincorporated Fairfax County, Virginia, US, the company is entirely owned by the Mars family.\n\n Tareyton is currently produced by R. J. Reynolds Tobacco Company, and can be found on the internet and specialty tobacco stores, but is no longer sufficiently popular to be stocked in many stores or receive marketing and advertising from the manufacturer.",
